<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-QMC says sees stable magnesium price.</title>
<headline>RTRS-QMC says sees stable magnesium price.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Queensland Metals Corp (QMC), which on Thursday announced a partnership with Ford Motor Co to develop a 90,000-tonne a year magnesium smelter, said it expected world magnesium prices to remain stable.</p>
<p>&quot;The price today is around about US$1.50 to US$1.60 (per pound). We'd expect that to continue roughly that way,&quot; QMC chairman Ian Howard-Smith told a news conference after the partnership with Ford was announced.</p>
</text>
